 A coding agent (polecat or equivalent) follows the steps in order. The
 molecule root bead IS the control bead — run state is recorded in its notes
-via `gc bd update <root-id> --notes "<key>: <value>"`.
+via `gc bd update <root-id> --append-notes "<key>: <value>"`.
+
+**Every note write in this formula is `--append-notes`, never `--notes`.**
+`--notes` REPLACES the field. The `implement` step reads `contract_path:`
+back off the notes two steps after `scaffold` wrote it, so a replacing write
+anywhere in between erases the only record of which file the loop is working
+on — and `gc bd update` still exits 0, so the loss surfaces as an
+unexplained "no contract_path on the root bead" at the implement gate rather
+than at the write that caused it. Appending also keeps the witness's and
+refinery's own annotations on a shared bead.
 
